00:34:52.360 --> 00:34:57.660
where we learn to live out and practice the grace and mercy of God. And something I want to encourage

00:34:57.660 --> 00:35:03.820
you with is, you know what, today, even maybe you're realizing, oh, why am I so critical?

00:35:04.820 --> 00:35:10.360
Why do I judge other people? Why do I think I'm better than them? Why do I have this mindset? Oh,

00:35:10.360 --> 00:35:16.480
what's wrong with me? The response to that is not to beat yourself up for being judgmental.

00:35:16.540 --> 00:35:22.680
The response to that is actually to turn again to the amazing grace of God where he transforms us

00:35:22.680 --> 00:35:29.100
with his kindness and his mercy. We will never change by beating ourselves up. We will never

00:35:29.100 --> 00:35:34.180
change by condemning or accusing ourselves. We will never change by judging other people or

00:35:34.180 --> 00:35:39.840
having them judge us. The way our hearts and our minds change is actually coming to God's

00:35:39.840 --> 00:35:47.020
amazing grace, and there we receive his kindness, his mercy, his forgiveness, and that sets us free

00:35:47.020 --> 00:35:52.660
from self-righteousness. It sets us free from judgment and criticism and condemnation. It sets

00:35:52.660 --> 00:35:58.880
us free from all of that to now be able to live with God and with one another in a different way.

00:35:59.600 --> 00:36:06.160
And really, when we get there, that's when we can start to understand what Paul wants to bring us

00:36:06.160 --> 00:36:13.160
too in our understanding of works, that we want to walk in good works in response to the gospel.

00:36:13.760 --> 00:36:18.260
We need to talk about walking in good works. I'll read verse 10 again. It says,

00:36:18.420 --> 00:36:24.480
for we are his workmanship created in Christ Jesus for good works, which God prepared beforehand

00:36:24.480 --> 00:36:30.260
that we should walk in them. Just so you know, in case I've shared this before, but when you see

00:36:30.260 --> 00:36:35.580
in the New Testament walk, to walk in something, that just means live. So it's really saying should

00:36:35.580 --> 00:36:41.140
live in them, should live in these good works. And we've just talked about, and let's say it for

00:36:41.140 --> 00:36:46.620
clarity again, verse 8 and 9, we just talked about our good works don't save us. Our good works

00:36:46.620 --> 00:36:51.820
don't save us. They have nothing to do with it, actually. So what is the role of good works in

00:36:51.820 --> 00:36:57.040
the Christian life then? If it's not to save us, and some of us are like, well, if I don't get

00:36:57.040 --> 00:37:03.680
anything out of it, why would I do it? If I don't earn something, if I don't prove something, if I'm

00:37:03.680 --> 00:37:08.700
not getting something honest, why would I do it? And here what God is wanting us to understand is

00:37:08.700 --> 00:37:15.540
that this is actually a response to his goodness and mercy in our lives. It's important. So let me

00:37:15.540 --> 00:37:20.920
give you a couple other reference points. Like we see this in James, right? Some of you are

00:37:20.920 --> 00:37:26.100
familiar with this. James 2.14, what good is it, my brothers, if someone says he has faith but does

00:37:26.100 --> 00:37:31.980
not have works? Can that faith save him? And by the way, some people read this and they think

00:37:31.980 --> 00:37:33.900
that James and Paul are disagreeing with each other,

00:37:33.960 --> 00:37:35.500
that they're butting heads, but they're not.

00:37:35.920 --> 00:37:37.640
What James is saying here is that a person

00:37:37.640 --> 00:37:39.540
with true saving faith in Christ

00:37:39.540 --> 00:37:42.680
will also display good works as the fruit of that.

00:37:43.040 --> 00:37:45.780
In fact, when Jesus would talk about things like this,

00:37:46.000 --> 00:37:48.540
he would use the language of fruitfulness.

00:37:49.540 --> 00:37:51.380
He would say something like in the Sermon on the Mount,

00:37:51.480 --> 00:37:53.880
Matthew 7, he says, so every healthy tree

00:37:53.880 --> 00:37:57.900
bears good fruit, but the diseased tree bears bad fruit.

00:37:58.320 --> 00:38:00.680
So we aren't saved because of good works,

00:38:00.680 --> 00:38:07.100
but we do good works because we're saved. That's the relationship here. And Jesus sees good works

00:38:07.100 --> 00:38:12.680
as good fruit, maybe in a John 15 kind of way, that when we're connected to him, when we're

00:38:12.680 --> 00:38:19.080
abiding in the vine, that then out of that comes the fruit of good works that come from our lives.

00:38:19.240 --> 00:38:23.940
So this is a relationship we need to get clear again. We are not saying our good works don't

00:38:23.940 --> 00:38:30.160
lead to salvation, but our salvation leads to good works. And here, what comes out all this,

00:38:30.160 --> 00:38:36.180
we find that our good works actually reflect God's workmanship. Our good works reflect God's

00:38:36.180 --> 00:38:40.420
workmanship. I don't know if some of you may have had an experience similar to this in some other

00:38:40.420 --> 00:38:45.660
way before, but one experience that I remember pretty well from my childhood is that as I was

00:38:45.660 --> 00:38:52.240
growing up, eventually I started outgrowing the bed that I grew up in. I had this like blue

00:38:52.240 --> 00:38:58.180
metal framed bed and eventually like I started growing and my feet hit the end of it and my head

00:38:58.180 --> 00:39:03.580
hit the head of it. And it was like, okay, I need a new bed. And I remember that my dad said, hey,

00:39:03.580 --> 00:39:10.220
Peter, why don't we make you a new bed? And I was like, okay, great. Like my dad liked building

00:39:10.220 --> 00:39:14.660
things. He liked making furniture and fixing stuff around the house. And so I was like, man, that

00:39:14.660 --> 00:39:19.500
sounds great to me. I would love to do that together. And so my dad actually drew up a design

00:39:19.500 --> 00:39:24.140
for the bed. And then he brought it to me. He said, hey, Peter, what do you think about this

00:39:24.140 --> 00:39:27.900
design? And I was like, oh, that's so cool. Can we do this and this? And I had some other ideas.

00:39:28.180 --> 00:39:30.440
He's like, okay, yeah, we changed the design, updated it.

00:39:31.080 --> 00:39:33.980
So we did the design, and then we went to the lumber yard together,

00:39:34.120 --> 00:39:37.300
and we bought all the materials, all the different boards that we would need,

00:39:37.420 --> 00:39:38.800
and then we started working on it.

00:39:38.880 --> 00:39:42.720
And I remember for, like, months, just whenever my dad had a free moment

00:39:42.720 --> 00:39:46.100
on a Saturday or something, we would go out to the yard

00:39:46.100 --> 00:39:48.020
where we had, like, this covered porch,

00:39:48.140 --> 00:39:50.500
and we would start working on putting this bed together,

00:39:50.620 --> 00:39:54.440
cutting the different pieces, shaping the joints and stuff like that.

00:39:54.440 --> 00:39:55.140
We did all that.

00:39:55.520 --> 00:39:58.360
And then there were some things that actually my dad didn't have the tools for.

00:39:58.820 --> 00:40:01.600
So we actually went to a good friend who was a neighbor of ours,

00:40:01.760 --> 00:40:03.760
an old Turkish guy named Samim.

00:40:04.180 --> 00:40:07.340
And we went to Samim's house, and in his garage he had a lathe

00:40:07.340 --> 00:40:09.980
where you could, like, carve things into wood as it spun.

00:40:10.500 --> 00:40:13.160
And we did that together, and he didn't let me touch it

00:40:13.160 --> 00:40:14.380
because that was, like, really dangerous.

00:40:14.960 --> 00:40:18.140
But I got to, like, you know, help and watch and hold things.

00:40:18.460 --> 00:40:19.820
And I remember just going through all that,

00:40:19.920 --> 00:40:23.100
finally putting the bed together and beginning to sleep on it.

00:40:23.740 --> 00:40:26.840
And every time that I went to sleep on that bed,

00:40:27.380 --> 00:40:30.520
partly there was a sense of like, we did that.

00:40:31.440 --> 00:40:32.680
Like, we did that together.

00:40:33.440 --> 00:40:35.980
There was a sense of connection that I got with my dad

00:40:35.980 --> 00:40:37.740
through doing things like that together.

00:40:38.460 --> 00:40:41.320
To me, this was a representation of his love for me.

00:40:42.140 --> 00:40:42.800
And this was something,

00:40:42.900 --> 00:40:44.680
even when I think about that friendship with our neighbor

00:40:44.680 --> 00:40:46.340
who was a good friend of our family's,

00:40:46.640 --> 00:40:48.220
it's like, yeah, we did this together.

00:40:49.020 --> 00:40:50.080
And when I looked at it, I was like,

00:40:50.140 --> 00:40:52.540
man, the carving in it, the design of it,

00:40:52.540 --> 00:40:58.300
like I felt really good that like that was something I got to be part of. And I share that

00:40:58.300 --> 00:41:03.780
because here when we see something like our good work reflects God's workmanship, we are his

00:41:03.780 --> 00:41:11.180
workmanship created for good works. I think this is God's heart toward us. Like just so you know

00:41:11.180 --> 00:41:16.320
that the word translated workmanship, it's a Greek word poiema. You might hear the word poem

00:41:16.320 --> 00:41:21.280
in that and that's accurate. That's where we get the word poem. And some translations might say

00:41:21.280 --> 00:41:28.440
we are God's poetry or we are God's poem or we are God's artistry or we are his masterpiece

00:41:28.440 --> 00:41:36.100
because it has the connotation of like God creating something in us and as he creates something in us

00:41:36.100 --> 00:41:44.100
we then get to join him in the things that he is doing. He has made us and he has then remade us

00:41:44.100 --> 00:41:50.620
in Christ through his redemptive work and now he did that with incredible creativity and skill

00:41:50.620 --> 00:41:57.620
And now when we serve God and others, we use the gifts and the skills that he has given us.

00:41:57.780 --> 00:41:59.780
We reflect his creativity.

00:41:59.980 --> 00:42:03.920
We reflect his glory and the redeeming work that he has done in us.

00:42:03.960 --> 00:42:05.280
That is a beautiful thing.

00:42:05.520 --> 00:42:07.700
That is God's heart for us.

00:42:08.380 --> 00:42:09.660
And so we join God.

00:42:09.820 --> 00:42:16.920
Our good works are a reflection of God's workmanship, but also our good works fulfill God's purposes in our lives.

00:42:17.780 --> 00:42:20.440
Like, notice that we find that God created us

00:42:20.440 --> 00:42:23.960
for good works and he also prepared good works

00:42:23.960 --> 00:42:24.840
for us to do.

00:42:25.720 --> 00:42:26.080
Like, do you know what?

00:42:26.100 --> 00:42:29.020
There's a purpose there in how God created us

00:42:29.020 --> 00:42:31.660
and there's a plan there that God actually

00:42:31.660 --> 00:42:35.560
has specific things for you and I to do

00:42:35.560 --> 00:42:38.280
to join him in what it is that he is doing.

00:42:38.520 --> 00:42:40.740
We learn from that God has a purpose for our lives.

00:42:41.360 --> 00:42:42.800
Your life is not meaningless.

00:42:43.340 --> 00:42:44.640
Your life is not hopeless.

00:42:44.820 --> 00:42:45.920
Your life has a purpose.

00:42:45.920 --> 00:42:48.300
Turn to somebody next to you, say, your life has a purpose.

00:42:50.200 --> 00:42:55.380
We need to remind each other of that because sometimes the world in us tells us it's hopeless,

00:42:55.580 --> 00:43:00.020
tells us it's pointless, tells us there is no meaning, there is nothing behind all of it.

00:43:00.080 --> 00:43:02.280
It's all vanity of vanities, right?

00:43:02.320 --> 00:43:07.700
The world will tell you that, but here in God's word, we find that there is purpose and meaning

00:43:07.700 --> 00:43:12.980
to our lives and that God saved us because he loves us and because he wants us to have

00:43:12.980 --> 00:43:18.300
the joy of joining with him in his good work. We talked about that. Some of you were there for

00:43:18.300 --> 00:43:23.560
experiencing God this past Friday night. We talked about that, that we want to see what God is doing

00:43:23.560 --> 00:43:30.460
around us and join him in the work that he is doing. And so think about that. As God has saved

00:43:30.460 --> 00:43:37.660
us from all the stuff he saved us from, and he has given us this good gift that's a real gift.

00:43:37.660 --> 00:43:44.260
you never have to pay for it. You never have to try to earn it. None of that. It's a real gift

00:43:44.260 --> 00:43:52.340
purely by his grace. As we receive that by faith, what would it look like to joyfully enter into the

00:43:52.340 --> 00:43:58.300
work of God and have the privilege of being part of his work in the lives of those around us,

00:43:58.340 --> 00:44:03.940
in the world around us? What could that look like? And that could be so many different things,

00:44:03.940 --> 00:44:05.440
and I'll talk about some in a second,

00:44:05.580 --> 00:44:07.300
but even here, many of you know

