00:49:01.400 --> 00:49:04.400
And maybe we have this sense of debt toward others.

00:49:05.400 --> 00:49:08.460
For some of us, we actually need to unlearn some things

00:49:08.460 --> 00:49:10.460
in the way that we grew up.

00:49:11.020 --> 00:49:14.180
And it's not because anyone was wronghearted toward us

00:49:14.180 --> 00:49:16.000
or trying to shape us in a wrong way.

00:49:16.520 --> 00:49:18.920
But maybe as we grew up, we learned to function

00:49:18.920 --> 00:49:23.680
more out of debt, more out of shame,

00:49:24.620 --> 00:49:27.360
more out of fear of what other people will think of us,

00:49:28.020 --> 00:49:30.500
more out of a sense that we have to prove ourselves somehow.

00:49:31.280 --> 00:49:34.680
And I think God really wants to set us free from that.

00:49:35.320 --> 00:49:37.160
That's what the Lord is trying to do.

00:49:37.440 --> 00:49:40.140
And when we do that, wow, then we can step out in faith

00:49:40.140 --> 00:49:44.480
and see what a joy and privilege it is to join God in his work.

00:49:45.080 --> 00:49:47.240
So again, good works are not a means of salvation,

00:49:47.240 --> 00:49:49.820
but a response of love toward God and others.

00:49:50.140 --> 00:49:51.140
And if we want to connect this

00:49:51.140 --> 00:49:52.860
to what we're talking about as a church this year,

00:49:53.100 --> 00:49:54.880
I would say that our higher calling

00:49:54.880 --> 00:49:57.820
is to receive God's grace and respond with good works.

00:49:58.520 --> 00:50:00.840
That our higher calling is to receive God's grace

00:50:00.840 --> 00:50:02.660
and then respond with good works.

00:50:02.860 --> 00:50:04.980
Make sure that that's how we're connecting

00:50:04.980 --> 00:50:06.240
with God in our hearts.

00:50:06.760 --> 00:50:08.600
And I want to say for some of you here today,

00:50:08.720 --> 00:50:09.920
and most of you here in this room,

00:50:10.280 --> 00:50:12.060
you've been followers of Jesus for a long time.

00:50:12.120 --> 00:50:13.700
Maybe this feels kind of like old news,

00:50:13.780 --> 00:50:15.680
but we're just reflecting on it in a fresh way today.

00:50:16.160 --> 00:50:17.820
I do want to give a specific invitation

00:50:17.820 --> 00:50:19.380
that there may be some of you here

00:50:19.380 --> 00:50:21.600
that have never placed your faith in Jesus before.

00:50:22.200 --> 00:50:23.880
Maybe you never connected the dots

00:50:23.880 --> 00:50:27.140
of why Jesus came and died on that cross

00:50:27.140 --> 00:50:28.440
and shed his blood.

00:50:29.060 --> 00:50:30.580
And you've heard that it's for you.

00:50:30.900 --> 00:50:32.580
It's for forgiveness of your sin

00:50:32.580 --> 00:50:34.620
and the way you've rebelled against God.

00:50:35.140 --> 00:50:36.940
And maybe today that is actually starting

00:50:36.940 --> 00:50:38.340
to click into place a little bit.

00:50:39.120 --> 00:50:40.320
If you're in that place today

00:50:40.320 --> 00:50:42.660
and maybe wondering and asking questions,

00:50:42.960 --> 00:50:44.480
I want to give you an invitation today

00:50:44.480 --> 00:50:46.120
to place your faith in Jesus,

00:50:46.900 --> 00:50:49.740
to believe today that Jesus did those things,

00:50:49.880 --> 00:50:50.740
dying on the cross,

00:50:50.900 --> 00:50:53.940
because you and I, we couldn't save ourselves.

00:50:54.520 --> 00:50:55.840
We couldn't fix ourselves.

00:50:56.360 --> 00:50:57.380
The debt was too great.

00:50:57.440 --> 00:50:58.520
We never could have paid it.

00:50:58.580 --> 00:51:00.140
We never could have figured it out on our own.

00:51:00.140 --> 00:51:03.440
And God saw you and I and the people around you,

00:51:04.060 --> 00:51:06.400
and he saw even before we asked for forgiveness,

00:51:07.400 --> 00:51:10.400
even before we tried to come to Jesus by ourselves,

00:51:10.600 --> 00:51:11.260
when we couldn't,

00:51:11.880 --> 00:51:14.300
Jesus saw us, and maybe the reason you're here

00:51:14.300 --> 00:51:16.420
is that God is reaching out to you

00:51:16.420 --> 00:51:19.220
and inviting you into this relationship with him.

00:51:19.500 --> 00:51:22.700
Today, I wanna invite you, give yourself to Jesus.

00:51:23.260 --> 00:51:26.180
Tell him today that you believe in what he's done for you,

00:51:26.460 --> 00:51:27.900
that you receive his forgiveness,

00:51:28.120 --> 00:51:29.940
that you're committing your life to following him.

00:51:30.280 --> 00:51:31.060
And I would encourage you,

00:51:31.160 --> 00:51:32.980
share about that with somebody next to you.

00:51:33.280 --> 00:51:34.000
Come up afterwards,

00:51:34.160 --> 00:51:35.400
share that with one of the prayer ministers.

00:51:35.540 --> 00:51:37.520
We'd love to pray with you and follow up with you.

00:51:37.840 --> 00:51:40.640
But let's make that our response to the Lord today.

00:51:40.640 --> 00:51:42.500
And for many of the rest of us here,

00:51:42.500 --> 00:51:45.340
and maybe you believed in Jesus a long time ago

00:51:45.340 --> 00:51:48.060
but today possibly you're seeing

00:51:48.060 --> 00:51:50.320
that there's still a need for more of God's grace

00:51:50.320 --> 00:51:50.960
in your life

00:51:50.960 --> 00:51:53.440
can I share with you one last quote from Martin Luther

00:51:53.440 --> 00:51:57.280
he wrote this long after those 95 theses

00:51:57.280 --> 00:51:59.860
he wrote for almost 20 years

00:51:59.860 --> 00:52:03.440
and I still feel the old clinging dirt

00:52:03.440 --> 00:52:05.420
of wanting to deal with God

00:52:05.420 --> 00:52:07.640
that I may contribute something

00:52:07.640 --> 00:52:10.880
so that he will have to give me his grace

00:52:10.880 --> 00:52:12.640
in exchange for my holiness.

00:52:13.260 --> 00:52:16.020
And still, I cannot get into my head

00:52:16.020 --> 00:52:20.140
that I should surrender myself completely to sheer grace.

00:52:21.300 --> 00:52:22.780
Martin Luther struggled with that.

00:52:23.180 --> 00:52:25.160
I'm guessing many of us here struggle with that.

00:52:25.640 --> 00:52:29.040
Today, can I encourage us to live in God's grace together?

00:52:29.200 --> 00:52:30.580
And maybe it would help today

00:52:30.580 --> 00:52:32.980
to do things like just invite God

00:52:32.980 --> 00:52:34.880
to change your heart and renew your mind.

00:52:35.380 --> 00:52:37.440
Just give that invitation to the Lord today.

00:52:37.560 --> 00:52:39.820
Say, God, I need you to work in me.

00:52:39.900 --> 00:52:41.180
I'm not gonna fix myself.

00:52:41.400 --> 00:52:43.040
I can't get this done on my own.

00:52:43.420 --> 00:52:45.180
Lord, I'm inviting you to work in me.

00:52:45.620 --> 00:52:47.300
And there, something I would encourage you with

00:52:47.300 --> 00:52:50.480
is respond to God's grace with active faith.

00:52:51.080 --> 00:52:53.000
Respond to God's grace with active faith.

00:52:53.240 --> 00:52:53.940
What does that mean?

00:52:54.720 --> 00:52:58.300
That means when you see that tendency in your heart

00:52:58.300 --> 00:53:00.400
not to respond with grace,

00:53:00.400 --> 00:53:04.500
but to respond with some kind of self-justification

00:53:04.500 --> 00:53:07.660
or something, do the opposite of that.

00:53:08.120 --> 00:53:09.640
Like, I could give you a quick example.

00:53:09.820 --> 00:53:13.320
I think a lot of us have these conversations where, you know, sometimes in a conversation,

00:53:13.480 --> 00:53:16.980
people try to like one up each other. Have you been in that kind of conversation before? It's

00:53:16.980 --> 00:53:20.720
kind of infuriating, isn't it? Like when you get into that and like one person tries to say

00:53:20.720 --> 00:53:25.380
something better than the other. Imagine you're in that conversation and someone's sharing with

00:53:25.380 --> 00:53:29.480
you some great thing that's happened in their life. And maybe there's something in you,

00:53:30.460 --> 00:53:34.640
there's something inside of you that you are already getting your response ready

00:53:34.640 --> 00:53:39.480
to share something that you have that's even better than what they shared.

00:53:39.820 --> 00:53:42.060
Just imagine, maybe it's hard to imagine,

00:53:42.560 --> 00:53:44.360
just imagine that maybe you're in that conversation

00:53:44.360 --> 00:53:46.440
and you see that desire in,

00:53:46.540 --> 00:53:48.300
ah, I want to share something even better about me.

00:53:49.300 --> 00:53:51.380
What if instead of doing that,

00:53:51.880 --> 00:53:55.080
you respond in active faith to God's grace

00:53:55.080 --> 00:53:56.400
and you say, you know what?

00:53:56.880 --> 00:53:59.920
Not only am I not going to try to one-up that other person,

00:54:00.700 --> 00:54:02.800
but I'm actually going to lift them up instead.

00:54:04.540 --> 00:54:07.060
I'm not going to respond to them by competing with them,

00:54:07.060 --> 00:54:08.200
trying to be better than them.

00:54:08.740 --> 00:54:10.540
I'm actually just gonna encourage them and say,

00:54:10.680 --> 00:54:11.640
wow, that's so great.

00:54:11.760 --> 00:54:13.560
I'm so happy that that went that way for you.

00:54:14.460 --> 00:54:16.060
Maybe you even take an opportunity

00:54:16.060 --> 00:54:17.660
to lift up somebody else as well.

00:54:18.140 --> 00:54:18.980
Like, man, it's something else

00:54:18.980 --> 00:54:20.360
I really appreciate about somebody.

00:54:21.280 --> 00:54:23.340
Like, that's what active faith looks like

00:54:23.340 --> 00:54:25.900
and where the gospel starts to really change

00:54:25.900 --> 00:54:28.680
our relationships, the way we respond to people.

00:54:29.200 --> 00:54:31.300
And lastly, just give and receive forgiveness.

00:54:31.820 --> 00:54:33.500
This is so huge, brothers and sisters.

00:54:34.140 --> 00:54:35.860
This is where we start to see the gospel

00:54:35.860 --> 00:54:37.400
really hitting home in our lives.

00:54:37.840 --> 00:54:39.400
And I want to encourage us, as a church,

00:54:39.680 --> 00:54:41.660
one of my biggest prayers for us is we be people

00:54:41.660 --> 00:54:44.420
who really learn to respond with love and grace.

00:54:45.160 --> 00:54:46.200
And that sometimes means,

00:54:46.460 --> 00:54:48.100
if you realize you've offended somebody,

00:54:48.820 --> 00:54:50.080
it means going to them and saying,

00:54:50.600 --> 00:54:51.540
will you please forgive me?

00:54:52.480 --> 00:54:53.740
And if somebody's offended you,

00:54:54.160 --> 00:54:55.760
maybe that means actually going to them

00:54:55.760 --> 00:54:57.820
before they even ask, because you know what?

00:54:57.820 --> 00:54:59.300
God didn't wait for you to ask him.

00:55:00.720 --> 00:55:02.220
Maybe that means going to them and saying,

00:55:02.320 --> 00:55:03.580
hey, before you even ask me,

00:55:03.800 --> 00:55:05.160
I want to offer you my forgiveness.

00:55:05.600 --> 00:55:07.120
I'm not going to hold this against you anymore.

00:55:08.080 --> 00:55:10.880
This is where the gospel starts to hit home in our lives.

00:55:11.440 --> 00:55:12.420
Can we stand together?

00:55:12.540 --> 00:55:14.520
We'll spend some time in response here this morning.
